  "prefLabel": "Puc 2502.06 Certificate",
  "priorExpiration": "2008-05-25",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 2502.06 “Certificate” means “certificate” as defined in RSA 362-F:2, III, namely “the record that identifies and represents each megawatt-hour (MWh) generated by an eligible renewable energy generating source under RSA 362-F:6.” The term “certificate” also includes the terms “renewable energy certificate” and “REC.”\n\nSource. #9037, INTERIM, eff 11-27-07, EXPIRED: 5-25-08\n\nNew. #9169, eff 6-3-08; ss by #10741, eff 12-5-14 (from Puc 2502.06); ss by #12473, eff 2-1-18 (formerly Puc 2502.05)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc2500.html"
